This repository contains no model weights. It works with, and in places is derived from, the following projects,
which keep their own licences.

Strata (https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Niko1221 and the Strata contributors. MIT License.
  - codecs/strata_codecs.py and engine/strata_decode.py are Python reimplementations of Strata's published decoders
    (C++ dequantizer and Metal shaders, commit 26350e4); codecs/FORMAT.md documents the format from that source.
  - engine/*.patch modify Strata's engine source at commit 26350e4 and are distributed as patches; the files they
    produce remain under Strata's MIT License. engine/build.sh mirrors Strata's CMake build.
  - codecs/test_codecs.py loads Strata's reference S_K codec (tools/squant/codecs.py) from a Strata checkout at run
    time to cross-check our decoder; that code is not copied here.
  - docs/serve-protocol.md describes the --serve protocol as implemented in Strata's ink_serve.h.

Inkling 2 Mini (https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini)
  Made by Thinking Machines Lab. Apache License 2.0, with a Model Acceptable Use Policy
  (https://thinkingmachines.ai/model-acceptable-use-policy/). The tools here operate on Strata's packed builds of this
  model, which users obtain separately; any model they produce is subject to the same licence and policy.

AtomicChat's abliteration LoRA for Inkling 2 Mini
  Apache License 2.0. The tools here read its directions to build the edited pack and the direction file; the LoRA
  itself is not included.

llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp)
  Copyright (c) the ggml authors. MIT License. Its llama-server served the reference model in the
  evaluation, and its gguf Python package is used (as a dependency, not copied) to read the LoRA.
